# Citation metadata for the specsr package.
#
# GitHub reads this file to render the "Cite this repository" button, and
# `preferred-citation` below is what that button offers first: the paper, which
# is what someone using the method should cite. The top-level block describes
# the software itself and carries the Zenodo concept DOI, for anyone who needs
# to reference a particular version of the code.
#
# Keep `version` and `date-released` in step with pyproject.toml on every
# release; the rest changes only when authorship or the paper's status does.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the paper below. To reference a
  specific version of the code, cite the Zenodo record.
title: "specsr: physics-informed super-resolution of JWST/NIRSpec prism spectra"
abstract: >-
  A physics-informed deep learning framework that super-resolves JWST/NIRSpec
  prism spectra towards medium-resolution grating quality, with a conditioning
  head that supplies a redshift estimate to the reconstruction.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aryana
    family-names: Haghjoo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3071-7143"
    email: ahagh010@ucr.edu
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of California Riverside
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21943196
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aryana-haghjoo/specsr"
url: "https://aryana-haghjoo.github.io/specsr/"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - spectroscopy
  - super-resolution
  - deep-learning
  - jwst
  - nirspec

